Z||000003||Hank is Here||01-22-2001||01:54 PM||||What all is in the kit?  How much does it cost?  I assume that it is a fairly simple setup||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||01-22-2001||06:54 PM|||| All the kit consists of are a pair of adapters that bolt the strut at the right angle in the tower. In order for these to work you'll have to have coilovers on the rear.  Mounting the '88 cradle on the car isnt hard,the back mounting holes need to be slotted and the front perches need to be moved slightly.check out Held Motorsports or Ryane Racing's website for more info.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dave@heldmotorsports.com||02-19-2001||09:58 PM||||correct, the conversion kit consists of<BR>strut adapters - but we also sell coil-<BR>overs, heavy duty radius rods, lateral<BR>links, toe links - essentially all that<BR>you would need to put an '88 cradle under<BR>an earlier car.<P>dave<BR>      <A HREF="http://heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>http://heldmotorsports.com</A> <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> All the kit consists of are a pair of adapters that bolt the strut at the right angle in the tower. In order for these to work you'll have to have coilovers on the rear.  Mounting the '88 cradle on the car isnt hard,the back mounting holes need to be slotted and the front perches need to be moved slightly.check out Held Motorsports or Ryane Racing's website for more info.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
